### Keep pinned access keys stable when recents come first

**Severity:** `medium`

When recent items are placed before pins, using `result.Count` renumbers every pinned Alt shortcut as history changes and can push pins beyond Alt+9. Assign pinned indexes from pinned order and place recent shortcuts after that reserved range so configured pins remain predictable.

```suggestion
        void AppendPinned(bool startsNewSection)
        {
            for (var i = 0; i < pinnedCount; i++)
            {
                result.Add(new ResolvedItem<T>(pinnedItems[i], true, i, startsNewSection && i == 0));
            }
        }

        void AppendRecent(bool startsNewSection)
        {
            for (var i = 0; i < recentCount; i++)
            {
                result.Add(new ResolvedItem<T>(recentItems[i], false, pinnedCount + i, startsNewSection && i == 0));
            }
        }
```

### Reserve configured pins beyond the display limit

**Severity:** `medium`

Stopping after the visible pin limit means later configured pins are never marked as owned by the pinned set. A hidden-over-limit pin can then reappear as a recent or regular command, so continue scanning all resolvable pins while only appending the configured visible count.

```suggestion
        void ResolvePinnedCommands()
        {
            var effectivePinnedCommandLimit = Math.Max(0, pinnedCommandLimit);
            foreach (var pinnedCommand in pinnedCommands)
            {
                var key = (pinnedCommand.ProviderId, pinnedCommand.CommandId);
                if (commandsByProviderAndId.TryGetValue(key, out var command) && featuredCommandKeys.Add(key))
                {
                    if (pinned.Count < effectivePinnedCommandLimit)
                    {
                        pinned.Add(command);
                    }

                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(pinnedCommand.CommandId))
                    {
                        featuredCommandIds.Add(pinnedCommand.CommandId);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
```

### Keep pinned commands in the pinned section

**Severity:** `medium`

Resolving in display order changes ownership: with recents before pins, a recently used pinned command is consumed by `Recent` and removed from `Pinned`, even though this feature promises unpinned recents. Resolve pins first for duplicate exclusion and apply visual section ordering only when composing the presentation.

```suggestion
        // Pins always own duplicates. Presentation order is applied after resolution so moving
        // the recent section does not turn pinned commands into recent commands.
        ResolvePinnedCommands();
        ResolveRecentCommands();
```

### Normalize invalid persisted placement values

**Severity:** `medium`

These enums deserialize arbitrary numeric values. The shelf treats unsupported values as hidden, but Home treats every non-hidden value as enabled and the settings ComboBoxes can receive an invalid index, so normalize persisted values at the model boundary.

```suggestion
    private RecentCommandsPlacement _recentCommandsOnQuickAccessShelf;

    public RecentCommandsPlacement RecentCommandsOnQuickAccessShelf
    {
        get => _recentCommandsOnQuickAccessShelf;
        init => _recentCommandsOnQuickAccessShelf = value is RecentCommandsPlacement.BeforePinned or RecentCommandsPlacement.AfterPinned
            ? value
            : RecentCommandsPlacement.Hidden;
    }

    private RecentCommandsPlacement _recentCommandsOnHome;

    public RecentCommandsPlacement RecentCommandsOnHome
    {
        get => _recentCommandsOnHome;
        init => _recentCommandsOnHome = value is RecentCommandsPlacement.BeforePinned or RecentCommandsPlacement.AfterPinned
            ? value
            : RecentCommandsPlacement.Hidden;
    }
```
